// Covered and bare keys (A:1229, TESTING TK-01): the bodies of TK-01-copy-join,
// TK-01-pick-param, TK-01-repoint, TK-01-owned-fields and TK-01-pick, which all
// compile; the caller's EN0614/EN0616 comes from stage 4's part test (plan d.8),
// which reads the bits checked here.
// Source:
//   class Pt { public xs: i64[] = []; public ys: i64[] = []; }
//   class Node { public val: i64[] = []; public kids: Node[] = []; }
//   class Holder { private view: &i64[]; private own: i64[] = []; private a: i64[] = []; }
//   lanes(p: &Pt, c: bool): [&i64[], &i64[]] { const s = p; const second = c ? &p.ys : &s.xs; return [&p.xs, second]; }
//   pick(p: &Node, c: bool): [&Node, &i64[]] { const q: &Node = c ? p : &p.kids[0]; return [q, &p.val]; }
//   repoint(let p: &Node, c: bool): &i64[] { const k = &p.kids[0].val; p = &p.kids[0]; return k; }
//   Holder.both(): [&i64[], &i64[]] { return [&this.own, &this.a]; }
//   Holder.pickView(c: bool): [&i64[], &i64] { const p = c ? &this.own : this.view; return [p, &this.view[0]]; }
// Shapes: a copy of a reference local as a reborrow moved into the binding (A:935,
// c.6), ternaries into the destination (c.5), an index's `len`/`check_bounds`
// guard run (c.4), a tuple literal of reborrows (c.5), a repoint (c.8), a field
// copy through `*_1` (A:935).
